task_outcome_detailed = f"""                                                                                            
DETAILED SCREENING RESULTS FOR CHUNK STUDIES 81-100                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
REVIEW PROTOCOL: Prophylactic platelet transfusion for prevention of bleeding in patients with haematological disorders 
after chemotherapy and stem cell transplantation                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
SELECTION CRITERIA: RCTs involving transfusions of platelet concentrates, prepared either from individual units of whole
blood or by apheresis, and given to prevent bleeding in patients with haematological disorders.                         
                                                                                                                        
=== INCLUDED STUDIES (6) ===                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
Study 83: "Prophylactic platelet transfusion in children with acute leukemia: A dose response study"                    
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: medium                                                                                  
Rationale: This study compares two dose levels of prophylactic platelet transfusions (low vs high dose) in              
thrombocytopenic patients with acute leukemia. While the abstract does not explicitly state 'randomized', it compares   
transfused vs nontransfused patients and different dose levels in what appears to be a controlled study design.         
Population matches (children with acute leukemia), intervention is prophylactic platelet transfusion, and outcome       
includes bleeding incidence.                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
Study 90: "Indications for platelet transfusion in children with acute leukemia"                                        
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high                                                                                    
Rationale: This is an RCT in 56 children with acute leukemia comparing prophylactic platelet transfusion (threshold     
20,000/mm3) vs therapeutic transfusion (only when bleeding occurs). The study directly addresses the review objective by
evaluating bleeding outcomes (time to first bleeding, number of bleeding episodes, days with bleeding) in patients with 
haematological disorders.                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
Study 96: "Clinical consequences of alterations in platelet dose: a prospective, randomized, double‐blind trial"        
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high                                                                                    
Rationale: This is a prospective, randomized, double-blind, multiple-crossover trial comparing lower-dose vs higher-dose
apheresis platelet transfusions in 46 patients undergoing high-dose therapy followed by hematopoietic progenitor cell   
transplantation. The study evaluates prophylactic transfusion outcomes including platelet count increments and          
transfusion-free intervals, which relate to bleeding prevention. Population matches (patients undergoing stem cell      
transplantation).                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
Study 97: "Randomized study of prophylactic platelet transfusion threshold during induction therapy for adult acute     
leukaemia: 10 x 109/L versus 20 x 109/L"                                                                                
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high                                                                                    
Rationale: This is a randomized single-institution trial comparing two prophylactic platelet transfusion thresholds     
(≤10,000/μL vs ≤20,000/μL) in 78 patients undergoing induction therapy for acute leukemia. The study directly addresses 
the review objective by evaluating bleeding episodes, transfusion requirements, and morbidity outcomes in patients with 
haematological disorders receiving chemotherapy.                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
Study 98: "Therapeutic efficacy and safety of platelets treated with a photochemical process for pathogen inactivation: 
the SPRINT Trial"                                                                                                       
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: medium                                                                                  
Rationale: This is a large RCT (SPRINT Trial) with 645 thrombocytopenic patients randomly assigned to receive           
photochemically treated vs conventional platelets. The primary endpoint was WHO grade 2 bleeding during platelet support
period. The study evaluates prophylactic platelet transfusion effectiveness for bleeding prevention, though the specific
haematological disorder status of all patients is not fully detailed in the abstract.                                   
                                                                                                                        
Study 100: "The prophylactic treatment of thrombocytopenic leukemic patients with platelets: a double blind study"      
Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high                                                                                    
Rationale: This is a double-blind randomized study in 18 patients with thrombocytopenia and acute leukemia comparing    
prophylactic platelet transfusion vs platelet-poor plasma. The study directly evaluates bleeding frequency as the       
outcome, affirming the value of prophylactic platelet transfusions. Population matches (acute leukemia patients) and    
intervention is prophylactic platelet transfusion.                                                                      
                                                                                                                        
=== EXCLUDED STUDIES (14) ===                                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
Study 81: "Measurement of bleeding severity: a critical review" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                             
Rationale: Critical review article summarizing methods for measuring bleeding severity, not an RCT of prophylactic      
platelet transfusion.                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
Study 82: "Perioperative platelet transfusion: recommendations of the Agence Francaise de Securite Sanitaire des        
Produits de Sante (AFSSaPS) 2003" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                           
Rationale: Professional consensus/guideline document presenting recommendations from AFSSaPS, not an RCT. Abstract      
explicitly states recommendations are 'not based on any randomized studies'.                                            
                                                                                                                        
Study 84: "Bedside filtration of blood products in the prevention of HLA alloimmunization: A prospective randomized     
study" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                                      
Rationale: While this is an RCT in patients with hematologic malignancy receiving platelet support, the primary outcome 
is HLA alloimmunization, not bleeding prevention. The intervention (bedside leucodepletion) focuses on preventing       
alloimmunization rather than optimizing prophylactic transfusion for bleeding prevention.                               
                                                                                                                        
Study 85: "Utilization of platelet transfusions in the intensive care unit: Indications, transfusion triggers, and      
platelet count responses" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                   
Rationale: Observational study of platelet transfusion utilization in general medical-surgical ICU patients, not        
specifically patients with haematological disorders undergoing chemotherapy or stem cell transplantation. Study design  
is retrospective/observational, not an RCT.                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
Study 86: "Delayed alloimmunization using random single donor platelet transfusions: a prospective study in             
thrombocytopenic patients with acute leukemia" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                              
Rationale: Randomized study comparing single-donor vs multiple-donor platelets in patients with acute leukemia, but     
primary outcomes are alloimmunization and refractoriness, not bleeding prevention. Does not address effectiveness of    
prophylactic transfusion for preventing bleeding.                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
Study 87: "A randomized controlled trial comparing plasma removal with white cell reduction to prevent reactions to     
platelets" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                                  
Rationale: RCT comparing plasma removal vs WBC reduction to prevent transfusion reactions in adults with hematologic    
disease. Primary outcome is transfusion reactions (fever, etc.), not bleeding prevention. Intervention targets reaction 
prevention rather than bleeding prevention.                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
Study 88: "Perioperative platelet transfusion. Recommendations of the French Health Products Safety Agency (AFSSAPS)    
2003" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                                       
Rationale: Duplicate/similar guideline document from AFSSAPS presenting expert recommendations, not an RCT. Abstract    
states recommendations are 'not based on any randomized studies'.                                                       
                                                                                                                        
Study 89: "Platelet transfusions in children: results of a randomised prospective cross‐over trial of plasma removal and
a prospective audit of WBC reduction" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                       
Rationale: Randomized crossover trial in children comparing plasma removal and WBC reduction, but primary outcome is    
febrile nonhemolytic transfusion reactions (FNHTRs), not bleeding prevention. Does not evaluate bleeding outcomes.      
                                                                                                                        
Study 91: "Economic consequences of alterations in platelet transfusion dose: analysis of a prospective, randomized,    
double‐blind trial" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                         
Rationale: Economic analysis/decision modeling study based on data from another trial, not a primary RCT. Evaluates cost
implications of platelet dose changes rather than clinical bleeding outcomes.                                           
                                                                                                                        
Study 92: "Comprehensive criteria for assessing therapy‐induced toxicity" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                   
Rationale: Methodology paper developing comprehensive criteria for assessing therapy-induced toxicity. Not a clinical   
trial of platelet transfusion and does not involve patients with haematological disorders receiving prophylactic        
platelet transfusions.                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
Study 93: "Platelet utilisation and the transfusion trigger: A prospective analysis" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)        
Rationale: Prospective observational analysis of platelet utilization practices at one hospital when transitioning      
transfusion triggers. Not an RCT; no randomization or control group. Describes practice patterns rather than testing an 
intervention.                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
Study 94: "Prophylactic platelet transfusion threshold during therapy for adult acute myeloid leukemia: 10,000/mL" -    
EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                                               
Rationale: Compares two time periods (1989-1993 vs 1994-1998) with different transfusion thresholds in adult AML        
patients. Historical cohort/quasi-experimental design, not an RCT. Patients were not randomized to threshold groups.    
                                                                                                                        
Study 95: "Use of leucocyte‐poor blood components and HLA‐matched‐platelet donors to prevent HLA alloimmunization" -    
EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                                               
Rationale: Compares three groups (leucocyte-poor components, standard components, and leucocyte-poor plus HLA-matched)  
for HLA alloimmunization outcomes. Primary outcome is alloimmunization, not bleeding prevention. Study design does not  
appear to be randomized.                                                                                                
                                                                                                                        
Study 99: "Accuracy of platelet counting haematology analysers in severe thrombocytopenia and potential impact on       
platelet transfusion" - EXCLUDE (high confidence)                                                                       
Rationale: Multicentre laboratory study evaluating accuracy of haematology analysers for platelet counting in severe    
thrombocytopenia. Not a clinical trial of platelet transfusion and does not involve patient outcomes related to bleeding
prevention.                                                                                                             
