confidence because while it's clearly an RCT with bleeding as primary outcome, the specific haematological disorder     
status of all patients is not fully detailed.                                                                           
                                                                                                                        
5. DUPLICATE HANDLING: Studies 82 and 88 appear to be the same guideline document published in slightly different       
formats; both were excluded as neither is an RCT.                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
All decisions follow the principle of being conservative when in doubt - including studies that may potentially meet    
criteria rather than excluding them prematurely.                                                                        
